## What it does

A skill is a directory with a `SKILL.md` instruction file and any companion files. A skill bundle collects those directories for publication. Rat-stack builds one bundle from `skills/`.

- The site serves the bundle over [MCP](/lore/mcp-is-another-surface) at `/mcp`. [Effect](/lore/effect-basics) 4.1.4 registers the skills with `McpServer.registerSkill`. The workspace CLI serves the same bundle over standard input and output.
- The [Executor index](/.well-known/agent-skills/executor/index.json) serves the same files over HTTP. Each entry lists `SKILL.md` first, then companion paths, with a version digest for the whole entry.
- Both channels publish the defensive [security audit skill](/skills/security-audit). The site leaves out supporting files that can assist exploit development.
- The [original discovery index](/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json) points to the Executor index with a `Link` header.

[joel.build](https://joel.build/mcp) is a second live example. Its server serves three skills over MCP.

## The standard

[SEP-2640](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/skills/overview) defines Skills over [MCP](/lore/mcp-is-another-surface). The Beta specification for `io.modelcontextprotocol/skills` is written against base protocol revision `2026-07-28`.

1. In `server/discover`, the server declares `capabilities.extensions["io.modelcontextprotocol/skills"]` and declares base `resources` support. The optional `directoryRead` setting enables directory listing.
2. `skills/list` returns entries without downloading file bodies. Each rat-stack entry includes the `SKILL.md` frontmatter as written, represented as JSON. Its manifest lists every file URI, `sha256:` digest, and byte size.
3. `skills/get` returns a single entry by its `SKILL.md` URI. A host can refresh an entry or retrieve one it has never listed.
4. The host loads files on demand with ordinary `resources/read` requests to `skill://rat-stack/<name>/<file>`. It verifies byte size and digest, and checks the loaded `SKILL.md` frontmatter against the entry.

For saved user approval, a version is the set of file URIs and their digests. Any change to that set revokes the approval. Matching a digest proves the bytes match the manifest. It does not tell you whether the instructions are safe.

### Client support on November 24, 2026

- [Claude Code](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/mcp#use-skills-from-mcp-servers): Public beta from 2.1.331. Use an interactive session and `/login` on an eligible plan. You need a supported model and a direct Anthropic connection. It excludes `claude -p`, the Agent SDK, custom base URLs, and `apiKeyHelper`.
- [VS Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/updates/v1_147#_skills-over-mcp): Enabled by default in 1.147.
- [MCP Inspector](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/blob/2.16.0/clients/cli/README.md#skill-verification---verify) verifies catalogs from its CLI. [fast-agent](https://github.com/evalstate/fast-agent/blob/main/docs/docs/mcp/skills-over-mcp.md) verifies and installs local copies. The [TypeScript SDK 2.4](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/pull/3047) offers `SkillsClient` in `ext/skills`.
- [Cursor](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/client-matrix) has no listed Skills extension support. The [extension's implementation list](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-skills/blob/main/docs/implementations.md) reports that ChatGPT and Codex rolled back skill import at plugin submission.

## How to check

Run the Inspector in verification mode. It downloads the listed files and checks them against the manifest and frontmatter.

```sh
pnpm dlx --package @modelcontextprotocol/inspector@2.16.0 mcp-inspector \
  --cli https://ratstack.sh/mcp --method skills/list --verify --require-digests
```

Expect exit code zero and this summary:

```text
Verified 23 skills and 87 files: no conformance errors.
```

An immediate repeat can hit the per-IP API limit. On `/mcp`, the server returns a JSON-RPC error that names `API_PER_IP`, with `Retry-After: 60` in the HTTP response. Wait a full minute before running the command again.

For the second channel, fetch the index and one file the index names:

```sh
curl -fsS https://ratstack.sh/.well-known/agent-skills/executor/index.json
curl -fsS https://ratstack.sh/.well-known/agent-skills/executor/durability/SKILL.md
```
